loom roster guards=29 green=29 red=0 seated=sow,tool_path
file template-manifest.bron the two stale classification rows repointed, each seated verdict carried forward unchanged
file tools/fixtures/sow_manifest_cover.sh the three verdicts read for what they are; shipping rows gated, defence in depth permitted and reported, doubling newly caught
file tools/fixtures/sow_manifest_cover_control.sh six behaviors on throwaway manifests -- one rests, one permitted, three red, one refuses
file construction/REDS.md row %165 booked and closed; two closed ranges folded to bring the pin back under bound
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri sow seated as the 29th guard, so the boundary guard is run rather than merely standing
file construction/ITINERARY.md the cadence state: projection and all four gates green, the force-push standing as the custody gate
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the seed is projected and all four gates read green (IDENT_CLEAN, NO_PERSONAL, M1_OK, seed_link GREEN), so the every-fifth-round cadence is ready and only the force-push remains. That push is named as a custody gate in the same breath that grants the cadence, so it waits for your word rather than my reading. Say ship the seed and it goes; otherwise the next lap takes the fold's step three, which has one open question waiting -- leave the 24 crypto/tally symlinks flat, or deepen every target one level.
